**Source:** AI Adoption Project Description for ABCDE Ltd. and risk register (10 risks)

## Risk matrix (from the risk register)
| ID | Category | Risk | Potential impact | Mitigation | Relevance to this project | Board evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R01 | Data Quality & Availability | Incomplete or unstructured data | Poor model performance and inaccurate outcomes | Perform early data audits and implement robust data governance | The project description mentions the importance of data quality for AI model performance, linking it to the risk of incomplete or unstructured data. | T006 |
| R02 | Integration Issues | Difficulty integrating AI with legacy systems | Delays in deployment and operational disruptions | Plan integration roadmap and use APIs/middleware | The integration of AI with existing workflows implies potential challenges with legacy systems, directly relating to the risk of integration issues. | None |
| R03 | Talent & Skills Gap | Lack of internal AI/ML expertise | Overreliance on external vendors and slow progress | Provide staff training and hire specialized talent | The project involves advanced AI technologies, highlighting the need for internal expertise and linking to the risk of a talent and skills gap. | T020 |
| R04 | Change Resistance | Employees resist adopting AI-driven workflows | Low adoption and reduced ROI | Strong change management and early engagement | The project aims to change workflows significantly, which may lead to employee resistance, connecting it to the risk of change resistance. | None |
| R05 | Ethical & Legal Concerns | Risks of biased models or data privacy violations | Legal repercussions and reputational damage | Involve legal early and implement fairness checks | The use of AI raises ethical concerns, particularly regarding data privacy, which is directly related to the risk of ethical and legal concerns. | T025 |
| R06 | Cost Overruns | Underestimation of AI development costs | Budget constraints and project delays | Set realistic budget and build in contingency funds | The project involves significant investment in AI, which could lead to cost overruns if not managed properly. | None |
| R07 | Unrealistic Expectations | Stakeholders expect immediate ROI | Disillusionment and loss of support | Align expectations and show quick wins | Stakeholders may expect immediate results from the AI adoption, linking to the risk of unrealistic expectations. | None |
| R08 | Model Performance Drift | AI models lose accuracy over time | Incorrect decisions and trust erosion | Regular retraining cycles and monitoring dashboards | The ongoing nature of AI model performance monitoring is crucial, connecting it to the risk of model performance drift. | T022 |
| R09 | Security Vulnerabilities | AI models targeted by adversarial attacks | Data breaches and operational risks | Adopt AI security best practices and penetration testing | The project description does not explicitly mention security, but the integration of AI raises concerns about potential security vulnerabilities. | T024 |
| R10 | Vendor Lock-in | Overdependence on a specific AI platform | Flexibility loss and future switching costs | Favor open standards and negotiate flexible vendor terms | The project may involve selecting specific AI platforms, which could lead to vendor lock-in, linking it to the associated risk. | T009 |

## Note
The assessment identifies several risks associated with data quality, integration, and stakeholder expectations, all of which are critical for the successful implementation of the AI adoption project.

The register has no likelihood or severity scores, so no scores are given.

